  "series": "GRAPHQL SCHEMA DESIGN",
  "date": "07/09/2026",
  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "The Schema Is the Contract",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Contract, Not Endpoint",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Schema = strongly typed graph of what a client may ask",
            "Server publishes it; the client queries against it",
            "Every field resolves to exactly one type",
            "No `any`, no untyped bag, no dynamic field set"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "type Query { me: User }",
            "type User {",
            "  id: ID!      # opaque identifier",
            "  name: String!",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Root Operation Types"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Root",
            "Purpose",
            "Required?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Query`",
              "reads",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "`Mutation`",
              "writes",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "`Subscription`",
              "event streams",
              "no"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`schema { query: Query, mutation: Mutation }` is optional",
            "Omit it and default root names are assumed",
            "Only `Query` must exist for a valid schema"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "SDL Vocabulary"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`type`, `input`, `enum`, `interface`, `union`",
            "`scalar` names a leaf; `directive` names an annotation",
            "SDL is the canonical text form of the type system"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Naming Discipline",
          "items": [
            "Type names are globally unique — no namespaces",
            "So `UserAddress`, never `Address` twice",
            "Names match `/[_A-Za-z][_0-9A-Za-z]*/`",
            "Leading `__` is reserved for introspection"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Docs vs Comments"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "\"\"\"A registered account.\"\"\"",
            "type User {",
            "  \"Stable primary key.\"",
            "  id: ID!   # this comment is dropped",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Checked Before Anything Runs",
          "text": "Validation is static: the query is checked against the schema before a single resolver executes. Validation phase precedes execution."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`__schema` and `__type` expose the schema at runtime",
            "That powers GraphiQL, codegen and client type safety"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "query ($x: String) { f(arg: $x) }",
            "# invalid if arg is String! and $x",
            "# has no default value"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "The Schema Is the Contract (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Authoring & Evolution"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Schema-first",
                "lines": [
                  "Write SDL by hand",
                  "Generate resolver stubs",
                  "SDL is the source of truth"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Code-first",
                "lines": [
                  "Write typed code",
                  "SDL emitted on build",
                  "Code is the source of truth"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Hold This Picture",
          "text": "The schema is a type graph; a query is a path selection through it returning a tree shaped like the query. It is also the versioning surface — additive is safe, removals and type changes break clients."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Leaves Of The Query",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Scalars resolve to a concrete value",
            "They are leaf types — no selection set allowed",
            "Five built-ins ship with every schema"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Scalar",
            "Serializes as",
            "Watch out"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Int`",
              "JSON number",
              "signed 32-bit only"
            ],
            [
              "`Float`",
              "JSON number",
              "IEEE-754, not money"
            ],
            [
              "`String`",
              "JSON string",
              "UTF-8 text"
            ],
            [
              "`Boolean`",
              "true / false",
              "—"
            ],
            [
              "`ID`",
              "JSON string",
              "opaque, no math"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Int` range is −2^31 to 2^31−1",
            "Outside it: a custom scalar or a `String`",
            "Money uses a `Decimal` scalar or integer minor units"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The `ID` Rule"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "user(id: 1)     # coerced to \"1\"",
            "user(id: \"1\")   # same value",
            "# ID equality is string equality"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Serializes as a String, signals opaque identifier",
            "Accepts Int or String input, coerces to String",
            "Never do arithmetic on an `ID`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Custom Scalars"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "scalar DateTime",
            "# SDL only names it — the server",
            "# supplies serialize / parseValue /",
            "# parseLiteral"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Hook",
            "Converts",
            "Side"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`serialize`",
              "internal to JSON",
              "output"
            ],
            [
              "`parseValue`",
              "variable to internal",
              "input"
            ],
            [
              "`parseLiteral`",
              "inline AST to internal",
              "input"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Ones You Will Write",
          "items": [
            "`DateTime` (ISO-8601), `UUID`, `URL`",
            "`EmailAddress`, `BigInt`, `JSON`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Validation Boundary",
          "text": "Throw inside `parseValue` and the request is rejected before any resolver runs — the scalar is your cheapest input guard."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Coercion Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Int` accepts an int literal only",
            "`Float` accepts int or float — the int is widened",
            "`String` never silently accepts a number"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The `scalar JSON` Tax",
          "text": "An escape hatch that destroys type safety, introspection value and codegen at once. Use it sparingly, if at all."
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Scalars: The Leaves of Every Query",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Sharp Edge",
          "text": "A custom scalar's semantics live in server code, not SDL. Two services can define `DateTime` incompatibly, so federation must align them by hand."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Object Type Anatomy",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "type User {",
            "  posts(first: Int = 10): [Post!]!",
            "}",
            "# name(arg: Type = default): Return @dir"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An object type is a named set of typed fields",
            "Only object types can carry a selection set",
            "Every query path must end at a scalar or an enum"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Arguments"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Arguments are per-field, not just per-query",
            "They express filtering, pagination and formatting",
            "A default value makes an argument effectively optional"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Never An Output Type",
          "text": "Argument types must be input types: scalars, enums, input objects and their list or non-null wrappers. `User` as an argument is illegal."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Input vs Output"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "`type` (output)",
                "lines": [
                  "Fields take arguments",
                  "Can implement interfaces",
                  "Returned, never passed in"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "`input` (input)",
                "lines": [
                  "Plain serializable fields",
                  "No arguments, no interfaces",
                  "Cycle-safe by nullability"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "input CreateUserInput { name: String! }",
            "type Mutation {",
            "  createUser(in: CreateUserInput!): User",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Resolvers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Signature is `(parent, args, context, info)`",
            "`parent` is the resolved value of the enclosing field",
            "No resolver? the engine reads `parent[fieldName]`",
            "Unselected fields never run — resolution is lazy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Selection",
            "Order"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Sibling fields on an object",
              "parallel"
            ],
            [
              "Mutation root fields",
              "serial, left to right"
            ],
            [
              "Nested fields",
              "after the parent resolves"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shape & Modularity"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Circular refs are normal: `User.posts`, `Post.author`",
            "`extend type Query { ... }` splits a root across files",
            "That split is the key to modules and federation"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Object Types and Fields",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The N+1 Tax",
          "text": "Nested object fields fan out one call per parent. Batch with a per-request DataLoader — do not flatten the schema to dodge it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Closed Set Of Values",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "enum Role { ADMIN EDITOR VIEWER }",
            "# leaf type — no selection set"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A fixed, validated set of symbolic values",
            "`SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` by convention",
            "`true`, `false` and `null` are forbidden as names"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Quoting Trips People"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "query { users(role: ADMIN) { id } }",
            "# variables JSON: {\"role\": \"ADMIN\"}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Inline enum literals are unquoted",
            "The same value is a quoted string as a JSON variable",
            "Server maps `ADMIN` to `1` or `\"admin\"` via a value map"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Free Tooling",
          "text": "Enums self-document in introspection: explorers render dropdowns and codegen emits a union of string literal types automatically."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Enum Or String?"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "`enum`",
                "lines": [
                  "Validated per request",
                  "Introspection plus codegen",
                  "Breaks when the set grows"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "`String`",
                "lines": [
                  "Add values, no schema change",
                  "No validation, no dropdown",
                  "Client guesses what is legal"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Closed sets — status, sort order — are enums",
            "Open sets — country codes, tags — are `String`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Change Safety"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Change",
            "Input pos.",
            "Output pos."
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Add a value",
              "safe",
              "breaking"
            ],
            [
              "Remove a value",
              "breaking",
              "safe-ish"
            ],
            [
              "Rename a value",
              "breaking",
              "breaking"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Output growth breaks exhaustive client switches",
            "`@deprecated(reason: \"...\")` works on values too",
            "Deprecated values stay valid, vanish from introspection"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Enums: Closed Sets of Values",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Seen Everywhere",
          "items": [
            "`SortDirection { ASC DESC }`",
            "`OrderStatus { PENDING SHIPPED CANCELLED }`",
            "`CacheControlScope { PUBLIC PRIVATE }`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Both Positions, Slowest Evolution",
          "text": "An enum used as an argument and as a return type inherits both rule sets, so it is the hardest type in the schema to change."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Not Integers",
          "text": "Never rely on ordinal position and never renumber internal mappings casually — the wire value is the name, nothing else."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Only Two Wrappers",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Non-Null `!` and List `[]` — all else is a named type",
            "Wrappers compose and read inside-out",
            "`[String!]!` is a non-null list of non-null strings"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Shape",
            "List",
            "Items"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`[String]`",
              "nullable",
              "nullable"
            ],
            [
              "`[String!]`",
              "nullable",
              "non-null"
            ],
            [
              "`[String]!`",
              "non-null",
              "nullable"
            ],
            [
              "`[String!]!`",
              "non-null",
              "non-null"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "[String]   # null, [], [\"a\", null]",
            "[String!]! # [] or [\"a\"] only"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Null Propagation"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Non-null is a promise: never `null` on success",
            "A non-null field that resolves null or errors bubbles up",
            "The null lands at the nearest nullable parent",
            "That parent's whole subtree is wiped"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "`Post.title` errors",
              "`[Post!]` non-null",
              "list nullified",
              "`feed` nullable",
              "null stops here"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Why Root Fields Stay Nullable",
          "text": "Bubble to a non-null root and `data` itself becomes `null` — one bad field nukes the response. A failing `me: User` must not erase a sibling `feed`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "List Resilience"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "List type",
            "One failed item"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`[Post!]!`",
              "whole list nullified"
            ],
            [
              "`[Post]!`",
              "item `null`, rest survives"
            ],
            [
              "`[Post]`",
              "item `null`, list may go null"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Non-Null and Lists: The Wrapping Types",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Errors always land in the top-level `errors` array",
            "Each carries a `path` to the exact failure",
            "`null` and \"not requested\" differ — unrequested is absent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Which Way Is Safe"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Position",
            "Nullable to non-null",
            "Reverse"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Output field",
              "safe",
              "breaking"
            ],
            [
              "Argument / input",
              "breaking",
              "safe"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Non-null argument, no default: required on every call",
            "Non-null argument with a default: may be omitted",
            "Direction inverts because inputs are supplied, not received"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Lists Are Not Pages",
          "text": "Lists are not paginated by nature — `[Post!]!` invites unbounded result sets. Anything that can grow needs a Connection with `first` and `after`."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Design Heuristic",
          "text": "Be liberal with nullable outputs at boundaries you do not control, like remote services. Be strict inside your own data."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Abstract, Shared Shape",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "interface Node { id: ID! }",
            "type User implements Node {",
            "  id: ID!",
            "  name: String!",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An interface declares a field set implementers must provide",
            "The implementer must include every interface field",
            "Interfaces express \"is-a\" with shared fields"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Querying One"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "node(id: $id) {",
            "  __typename",
            "  id                 # shared field",
            "  ... on User { email }",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Shared fields are selectable without a fragment",
            "Type-specific fields need an inline or named fragment",
            "`__typename` discriminates and keys the normalized cache"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Interfaces: Shared Shape, Many Implementations",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Server Must Discriminate",
          "text": "Supply `resolveType` on the interface, or `isTypeOf` on each type. Without one, execution errors at runtime."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Implementer Freedom"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Change on implementer",
            "Legal?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Add extra fields",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "Return a subtype",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "`String` to `String!`",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "`String!` to `String`",
              "no"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Covariant returns: narrower or more non-null is fine",
            "Never remove or narrow an interface field incompatibly",
            "`type User implements Node & Actor` — ampersand-separated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "interface Resource implements Node {",
            "  id: ID!     # must re-declare it",
            "  url: String!",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The `Node` Pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`node(id: ID!): Node` refetches any object by global ID",
            "One entry point, globally unique identifiers",
            "The basis of Relay's normalized cache"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Wide Blast Radius",
          "text": "Every interface field is a contract on all implementers — adding one to a widely implemented interface touches every type at once."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Sharp Edges",
          "items": [
            "An interface with no implementers is legal SDL",
            "It can never resolve to anything at runtime",
            "Skip `__typename` and Apollo or Relay caches wrongly"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "One Of These Types",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "union SearchResult =",
            "    User | Post | Comment"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A value is exactly one of the listed members",
            "Members must be object types",
            "No scalars, enums, interfaces, unions or inputs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Selecting From A Union"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "search(q: $q) {",
            "  __typename",
            "  ... on User { name }",
            "  ... on Post { title }",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Unions declare no common fields at all",
            "Every field selection needs an inline fragment",
            "`__typename` is the one field selectable with no fragment"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Same Runtime Duty",
          "text": "Like interfaces, a union needs server-side `resolveType` to map a runtime value onto a member type."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Unions: One Field, Unrelated Types",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Union Or Interface"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "`interface`",
                "lines": [
                  "Shared fields, \"is-a\"",
                  "Query common fields directly",
                  "Contract on implementers"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "`union`",
                "lines": [
                  "No shared fields, \"one-of\"",
                  "A fragment per member",
                  "Members stay unrelated"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Growth Breaks Clients",
          "text": "Adding a member is breaking in practice: existing clients have no fragment for it and render an empty object. Ship a fallback branch and treat unknown `__typename` as a degraded render, not a crash."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Errors As Data"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "union CreateUserResult =",
            "    CreateUserSuccess",
            "  | EmailTaken",
            "  | RateLimited"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The `errors` array is untyped and loses non-null guarantees",
            "A result union keeps failure modes in schema and codegen",
            "Give members `interface Error { message: String! }`",
            "Clients then render any failure generically"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Where Unions Fit",
          "items": [
            "Search results",
            "Feeds and activity streams",
            "Notification lists"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "No Input Unions",
          "items": [
            "The spec has no input union type",
            "Emulate with a one-of input object",
            "Many members force long brittle client queries",
            "Prefer an interface when types truly share fields"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Request Lifecycle",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "parse to AST",
              "validate",
              "coerce variables",
              "execute",
              "format response"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Parse and validation errors return before execution",
            "That response has `errors` and no `data` key at all",
            "A bad variable is a request-level error, not a field error"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
